                "name": "The sump gallery",
                "description": "A narrow gallery runs above a black sump, its rim ringed with iron grating. Dart-slots pock the inner wall at chest height, angled down the length of the walk. Whoever cut them meant them for whoever came to skim the sump: the tithe-keeps did not trust their own skimmers.",
