                "id": "5",
                "name": "The tithe vault",
                "description": "A cell barely three paces deep, its door faced with the same river stone as the wall so that it vanishes the moment it shuts. The tithe box is a squat iron thing bolted through its base into the flagstones, and somebody has levered at the lid until the hasp tore half out of the metal. Green flakes of the wax that once sealed it lie scattered where they fell.",
